    <briefdescription>
<para>Factory for creating projects from built-in or custom templates. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Template instantiation is atomic with respect to object creation: if schema validation or any object-creation step fails, all previously created objects are rolled back before the error is returned.</para>
<para>Template schema validation is always performed before any objects are written to storage. Instantiation of an invalid template definition returns a <computeroutput><ref refid="structthemis_1_1projects_1_1_template_instantiation_result" kindref="compound">TemplateInstantiationResult</ref></computeroutput> with <computeroutput>ok=false</computeroutput> and a descriptive error message — no partial state is written.</para>
<para>Thread-safety: all methods are thread-safe. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
